🏥 Hospital Admission Readiness Simulator
You are a Hospital Admission Coordinator.
There's a patient. There's insurance. There's a PA. There's a physician. And the clock is running. ⏱️
Can the patient be admitted — or not?
This isn't just a form. It's a weighted decision engine.
🔴 Prior Authorization — 25% weight
Approved? Pending? Denied? Every branch has its own path — follow up, upload docs, file an appeal, and if the appeal gets denied too? Escalate to Medical Director or IRO.
🟡 ICU + Denied PA = hard cap at 65%
You cannot reach 90% through admin tasks alone. That's the reality of healthcare operations.
📋 CMS 2-Midnight Rule — fires automatically when Observation is selected
MOON notification, SNF eligibility, cost-sharing differences — all documented inline.
🔬 InterQual / Milliman criteria — auto-triggers for Acute MI and CHF
Documentation must meet medical necessity thresholds before UR review. No shortcuts.
Score Weighting:
PA 25% · Clinical Docs 20% · Physician Orders 20% · Insurance 15% · Consent 10% · Bed 10%
≥ 90% → ✅ ADMIT — full summary + post-admission checklist
< 90% → ⚠️ NOT READY — exact missing items + required actions listed
≥ 75% → Governance Snapshot unlocks:
PA turnaround avg: 3–5 days · Inpatient denial rate: ~8–10% (CMS) · PA rework cost: ~$11/transaction (CAQH)
Care Coordination Cards include:
👨‍⚕️ Attending · 📋 Case Manager · 🏥 Nursing · 🔍 Utilization Review (InterQual, Milliman, concurrent review) · 🚪 Discharge Planner
Risk tracking across: Documentation · Insurance · Bed · Clinical
Clinical Risk is weighted highest for Acute MI, CHF, and ICU admissions.
9-milestone timeline that updates in real time as you complete each workflow action.
Single-file HTML. Zero backend. Zero database.
Pure logic, weighted scoring, and real healthcare workflow — in one simulator.
Because hospital admissions aren't bureaucracy for the sake of it — every checkbox protects a patient. 🩺
